{"id": "section-body-04937", "title": "Management of hiv and aids", "chapterId": "chapter-six", "blocks": [{"id": "body-04937", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading3", "text": "CHAPTER SIX MANAGEMENT OF HIV AND AIDS", "runs": [{"text": "CHAPTER"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "SIX "}, {"text": "MANAGEMENT"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "OF"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "HIV"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "AND"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "AIDS"}], "level": 3}, {"id": "body-04938", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "HIV is an RNA retrovirus which enters and multiplies in the host cells in a multistep process. In Tanzania HIV infection is mainly caused by HIV-1, dominated by sub-types, A, C, D, and their recombinants. Clinical features are usually due to immune system suppression.", "runs": [{"text": "HIV is an RNA retrovirus which enters and multiplies in the host cells in a multistep process. In Tanzania HIV infection is mainly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "caused"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "HIV-1,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "dominated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "by"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sub-types,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "A,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "C,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "D,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "their"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recombinants."}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "features"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "are"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "usually"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "due"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "immune system suppression."}]}, {"id": "body-04940", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Normal", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "Presentation", "bold": true}]}, {"id": "body-04941", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Fever, diarrhoea, weight loss, skin rashes, sores, generalized pruritis, altered mental status, persist